    "narrative": "The Austin Waves lineup is headlined today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Kyle Tucker** (81.26), both of whom present elite upside against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits immensely from a plus-matchup against Littell, with the projection model heavily weighting his position at the top of the order and his high-volume sprint speed, which remains vital in our pursuit of the scarcity-driven SB category. **Kyle Tucker** enjoys a massive boost from facing Kochanowicz, with the park factors and SP skill metrics aligning to make him our most reliable power-speed threat. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.73) and **Jackson Merrill** (68.69) represent strong secondary plays; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives on a favorable platoon edge against Baz, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages his leadoff spot to maximize opportunities against the hittable Hancock.\n\nThe benching of **Coby Mayo** (49.85) was the most difficult decision of the day, as he narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient profile of **Brady House**. While **Coby Mayo** faces the same favorable matchup against Littell as **Gunnar Henderson**, his position in the bottom third of the batting order and a slight penalty for facing an elite catcher reduced his efficiency floor below our established threshold. We are also monitoring **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 46.72 is trending near our marginal line; despite his #2 hole, the high-skill profile of Early creates a significant obstacle. We remain cautious of the Elite Hold SP tags attached to **Gunnar Henderson**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jackson Merrill**, as facing catchers with elite pop times will require aggressive, calculated baserunning today to secure our necessary SB totals.",
